Third-party notices
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PCOV
----

`ext/pebble.c` takes its set of ignored opcodes, and the line rules that go with
it, from PCOV (https://github.com/krakjoe/pcov), Copyright (c) The PHP Group,
author krakjoe, which is under version 3.01 of the PHP License
(http://www.php.net/license/3_01.txt). The same rules keep the executable lines
of this tracer identical to PCOV's.

This product includes PHP software, freely available from
<http://www.php.net/software/>.

PCOV is also an alternative backend at run time: with the pebble extension
absent, `src/Collector.php` calls PCOV's public PHP functions. That use does not
include or change PCOV's code.

Runner image
------------

The image in `docker/runner/` installs PHP, PCOV and the database servers from
distribution packages. Each keeps its own license, which the package files under
`/usr/share/doc` in the image carry.
